>>
>> It'd be also nice if you could define the syntax of this new cmavo in PEG
>> but we all believe that it wouldn't be ambiguous syntactically so defining
>> in PEG is not a must.
>>
>> What doesn't work for others might work for you and then more people.
>>
>
> As my skill improves, I imagine I will inevitable do so. But that will
> take some time yet. In the mean time, what unused cmavo are left that I
> could use?
>
Probably you would want cmavo in CV'Vi space where C is a consonant and V
is a vowel.

Check if a given cmavo isnt defined yet here:
e.g.
http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/be'ei
See? {be'ei} hasn't been yet defined.
You may try others.



